"Snail bait would fit into the same category, so any paddocks that have been baited for snails, growers should just be really vigilant to make sure that that bait's hit the ground and it's not hung up on the plant so that it's not coming through in their harvested sample," he said.
Waikerie dryland farmer Brenton Kroehn says the decision will not have a huge impact on his business, as he usually only delivers a small amount of grain to the Waikerie facility.
