Kenny returned to office in May as head of a government that is due to run until the end of 2018. But he has said he will not lead his Fine Gael party into the next election - though without committing to when he will stand down.
Lawmakers from the center-right party said planning for Kenny's departure was brought up for the first time at an internal Fine Gael meeting on Wednesday, a day before a poll showed it trailing rival Fianna Fail by nine percentage points.
